OL,3,CProbation officers threaten to strike
OL,4,Cin protest against early release scheme
OL,6,FProbation officers have voted
OL,7,Foverwhelmingly in favour of potential
OL,8,Fstrike action in protest at the
OL,9,Fgovernment's early release scheme.
OL,11,FAround 5,000 people are expected to be
OL,12,Freleased early under sentencing
OL,13,Fchanges due to take effect in October,
OL,14,Fin a bid to tackle jail overcrowding.
OL,15,FThey will need to be managed in the
OL,16,Fcommunity by probation staff.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31802
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786493896
OL,3,CProbation officers threaten to strike
OL,4,Cin protest against early release scheme
OL,6,FNapo, the probation union, said the
OL,7,Fsystem is already struggling to cope,
OL,8,Fand that a bigger workload will put
OL,9,Fpublic safety at risk. It said 90% of
OL,10,Fits members had backed potential
OL,11,Findustrial action.
OL,13,FThe Ministry of Justice said it was
OL,14,F"disappointed" by the outcome of the
OL,15,Findicative ballot, having agreed a pay
OL,16,Fincrease earlier this year.
OL,26,@vD@AOUvD@NO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786493896
OL,3,CProbation officers threaten to strike
OL,4,Cin protest against early release scheme
OL,6,FNapo national chair Ben Cockburn said:
OL,7,F"This ballot wasn't about members
OL,8,Fbeing too busy. It was professionals
OL,9,Fwarning they cannot protect the public
OL,10,Fproperly when there are not enough
OL,11,Fpeople to do the work.
OL,13,F"Probation staff make decisions every
OL,14,Fday with life-changing consequences
OL,15,Ffor the people we work with, victims
OL,16,Fand the public. If excessive workloads
OL,17,Fprevent those decisions being made
OL,18,Fproperly, the consequences can be
OL,19,Fdevastating.
OL,26,@oD@AOUuD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31804
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786493896
OL,3,CProbation officers threaten to strike
OL,4,Cin protest against early release scheme
OL,6,F"The government cannot keep treating
OL,7,Fprobation as the place where the
OL,8,Fconsequences of failures elsewhere in
OL,9,Fthe criminal justice system are
OL,10,Fdumped. If you overload probation, you
OL,11,Fincrease risk. It really is that
OL,12,Fsimple."
OL,14,FMinisters have said #700 million of
OL,15,Finvestment in the Probation Service by
OL,16,F2028 will mean tens of thousands more
OL,17,Foffenders can be tagged and monitored
OL,18,Fin the community.
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@HO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
